<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Lesson 5 - Trendlines & Channels</title>

    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #0b1812;
            color: white;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: auto;
            padding: 25px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #19e875;
        }

        .card {
            background: #0b3d2e;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .card h2 {
            color: white;
        }

        .card p {
            color: white;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        .lesson-image {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 600px;
            display: block;
            margin: 15px auto;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        .back-btn {
            display: inline-block;
            background: #19e875;
            color: #07130d;
            padding: 10px 18px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <a href="/lessons" class="back-btn">← Back to Lessons</a>

    <h1>📈 Lesson 5: Trendlines & Channels</h1>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>What Is a Trendline?</h2>

        <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='images/trendline.jpg') }}"
             class="lesson-image">

        <p>
            A trendline is a line drawn on a price chart to connect
            important highs or lows. It helps traders see the general
            direction of the market.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>📈 Uptrend Trendline</h2>

        <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='images/uptrend-trendline.jpg') }}"
             class="lesson-image">

        <p>
            An uptrend happens when price is generally making higher
            highs and higher lows. An upward trendline can be drawn by
            connecting important higher lows.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>📉 Downtrend Trendline</h2>

        <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='images/downtrend-trendline.jpg') }}"
             class="lesson-image">

        <p>
            A downtrend happens when price is generally making lower
            highs and lower lows. A downward trendline can be drawn by
            connecting important lower highs.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>What Is a Channel?</h2>

        <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='images/channel.jpg') }}"
             class="lesson-image">

        <p>
            A channel is formed by two roughly parallel lines that
            contain price movement. It can help traders identify the
            direction and boundaries of a market move.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>What Is a Trendline Break?</h2>

        <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='images/trendline-break.jpg') }}"
             class="lesson-image">

        <p>
            A trendline break happens when price moves through a
            trendline. It may be a sign that the current market
            movement is weakening or changing, but traders should
            look for confirmation.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>💡 Important Note for Beginners</h2>

        <p>
            Trendlines are useful tools, but they are not perfect.
            Price can temporarily break a trendline and continue in
            the same direction. Always combine trendlines with other
            forms of analysis.
        </p>
    </div>


<form action="/complete-lesson/5" method="POST" style="text-align:center; margin-top:30px;">
    <button type="submit"
            style="background:#19e875; color:#07130d; border:none; padding:12px 20px; border-radius:8px; font-weight:bold; cursor:pointer;">
        ✅ Mark Lesson 5 as Completed
    </button>
</form>

</div>

</body>
</html>

